nodes.prompt:
Brand: {{brand.brand_name}} — {{brand.brand_summary}}
Voice: {{brand.voice_tone}}
Value props: {{brand.value_props}}
Audience: {{brand.target_personas}}

Pain: {{inputs.pain}}
Turn: {{inputs.turn}}
Payoff: {{inputs.payoff}}
CTA: {{inputs.cta}}

Cast ONE person from the target audience and write a 3-beat story they film themselves: beat 1 is the pain with no product in sight, beat 2 is the turn with the product in use, beat 3 is the payoff and the CTA.

`actor` must pin identity down hard enough to repeat: apparent age, build, hair, face details, exact clothing including colour and fabric, and the specific place with named objects in it.

`master_frame_prompt` is a still-image prompt for the neutral establishing frame of this person in their space. Describe only the person, wardrobe, setting and light — no camera brand names, no quality adjectives, no text.

For each of the 3 shots write:
- `frame_prompt`: an EDIT instruction on the master frame, not a new scene. Always start with "Same person, same hair, same clothes." then change expression, posture, what they are holding, and the part of the room we see. Beat 1 should look worn down, beat 3 should look relieved.
- `motion_prompt`: what happens in the 6 seconds AFTER that frame — action and delivery only. Include the spoken line in double quotes.
- `line`: just the spoken words, at most 14 words so it fits in 6 seconds.

`on_screen_text`: one caption per beat, at most 5 words each.
